Z||000012||Robert||12-20-2000||02:53 PM||||I paid $225 for the set of two from PISA a couple of years ago.  I just checked in the 1999 issue of the BIG Fiero Parts Book, and they were still listed at that price.<BR>The fit was just ok, meaning you need to do some trimming and bending.  You also need to drill your own mounting holes.<BR>These scoops are fiberglass; I have heard that the rubber ones are easer to work on, but harder to find.<BR>I personally think the Mecham style is the best looking of the bunch, especially with yellow paint.<BR>Here is a current photo of my car, after almost two years of daily driving.<P>Funny story…..  The other night at the CFOG Christmas dinner, someone asked me what I was going to do next to my car.  I replied; “Nothing, I'm done”.  He was shocked, said he has never heard a Fiero owner say that before…   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_in_Fall.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||10
